id: text/set-from-hex/0001
area: text
op: FromHex into a destination
in: str:"aaZZ" int:0
out: value: str:"0/0/"
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: setFromHex parses its whole input before honouring the destination's length, so a character past the bytes that fit, which the specification never reads, raises SyntaxError where it answers { read, written }. Answered by Broiler.JS docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md, SJL-5.5 (the text area's record; the correspondence's row B1).
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-fromhex spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-uint8array.prototype.setfromhex ref:textref@1
script: (function () { var t = new Uint8Array(0); try { var r = t.setFromHex("aaZZ"); return r.read + "/" + r.written + "/" + Array.prototype.join.call(t, ","); } catch (e) { return e.name + "/" + Array.prototype.join.call(t, ","); } })()
since: 10

